## 0.1 GLOBAL MODIFIERS

| Flag | Action |
|------|--------|
| `--trace` | Pass to subagent envelope; subagent loads `debug-protocol.md` |
| `--pause` | When used with `/orchestrate`\|`/o`: stop after each phase for user inspection instead of auto-chaining |
| `--no-standards` | Pass to subagent envelope; subagent skips standards loading |
| `--no-jira` | Pass to subagent envelope; subagent skips Jira payload generation |
| `--python` | Set Language Context to PYTHON |
| `--preview` | Walk the phase chain without spawning subagents or modifying files; report the planned execution and run system validation (MCP, vault, registry, hub workspace). Applies to `/o` and `/d`. See `agent-orchestrator.md` §8 |
| `--jira-auto` | Skip Jira confirm-always pause; process payloads immediately. Available on `/o`, `/d`, `/jira` |
| `--dac` | Route to DaC Track agents (Structurizr DSL triplet unless paired with `--excalidraw` / `--e`) |
| `--excalidraw` | With `/dac spec|code|review`: route to Excalidraw DaC — read `.cursor/agents/excalidraw-dac.md`, canonical `docs/_ai_system/agents/agent-excalidraw-dac.md`; **do not** combine with `/dac deploy` in the same invocation |
| `--e` | Alias for `--excalidraw` |
| `--project [name]` | Set Active Project explicitly (see Step 0.7) |

---

## 0.2 VERSION CHECK — Deferred to subagents

Version and Jira staleness checks are handled by subagents, not the main chat.

---

## 1. CONTEXT LOADING — Deferred to Subagents

Standards, knowledge maps, and project rules are loaded by subagents, not the main chat. Each `.cursor/agents/*.md` file embeds self-loading instructions when those agents exist. The main chat only resolves the Task envelope fields.

---

## 2. ROUTING TABLE

> **PRIORITY:** Shortcuts are PRIMARY triggers. Inference is SECONDARY.

### ➤ SYSTEM OPERATIONS

| Shortcut | Agent | Inference Trigger |
|----------|-------|-------------------|
| `/check` | Check Agent (`agent-ops-check.md`) — **deprecated**; use `/o --preview` or `/d --preview` | "system check", "health check" |

### ➤ HUB & PROJECT OPERATIONS

| Shortcut | Agent | Inference Trigger |
|----------|-------|-------------------|
| `/onboard [project-name]` | Onboard Agent (`agent-ops-onboard.md` — **M1-P8**) | "register project", "onboard", "add project to Cuebert", "create hub project entry" |
| `/update` | Update Agent (`agent-ops-update.md`) | "update cuebert hub", "pull latest cuebert", **"rescan project"**, **"refresh project profile"** |
| `/update [project-name]` | Update Agent (`agent-ops-update.md`) | Same as `/update`, scoped to **project profile re-scan** on the hub |

### ➤ ORCHESTRATED ENGINEERING (Multi-Phase Pipeline)

> `/orchestrate` (alias `/o`) runs the full Spec → Code → Review → QA → QA Resilience pipeline via the Orchestrator. QA is mandatory per protocol (exceptions only when the active agent file documents hub-only meta work). It auto-chains by default — no user pause between phases unless `--pause` is specified or a circuit breaker trips.

| Shortcut | Alias | Behavior |
|----------|-------|----------|
| `/orchestrate [feature]` | `/o [feature]` | Full pipeline: Spec → Code → Review → QA → QA Resilience (auto-chain) |
| `/orchestrate --spec [feature]` | `/o --spec` | Start at Spec phase, chain forward |
| `/orchestrate --code [slug]` | `/o --code` | Start at Code phase (plan must exist), chain forward |
| `/orchestrate --review [slug]` | `/o --review` | Start at Review phase, chain forward |

**Routing:** On `/o`, the Supervisor loads the Orchestrator agent rules by reading `docs/_ai_system/agents/agent-orchestrator.md` into the main chat context. The Orchestrator then takes over the main chat and spawns phase subagents directly via `Task(subagent_type: "generalPurpose")`. Do NOT spawn the Orchestrator itself as a subagent — it runs in the main chat so it can reliably spawn and chain phase Tasks without nesting.

### ➤ DEPLOY HARNESS (Separate from `/o`)

> `/deploy` (alias `/d`) is a **separate harness** from `/o`. It is NOT a phase within the orchestration pipeline — it is invoked explicitly when the user decides to prepare for deployment. The Production Readiness Register (accumulated during `/o` runs as INFO-level findings) serves as the bridge.

| Shortcut | Alias | Behavior |
|----------|-------|----------|
| `/deploy` | `/d` | Full deploy pipeline: Production Readiness (REJECT mode) → Security → Jira Sync → Memory Commit → Checkin Log |
| `/deploy --preview` | `/d --preview` | Preview deploy pipeline without executing |

**Routing:** On `/d`, the Supervisor loads the Deploy Harness agent rules by reading `docs/_ai_system/agents/agent-deploy.md` into the main chat context (same pattern as `/o` with `agent-orchestrator.md`). The Deploy Harness then spawns phase subagents.

**Modifiers:** `--pause`, `--skip-jira`, `--skip-memory`, `--preview`, `--jira-auto`

### ➤ DIRECT ENGINEERING (Single-Phase, No Orchestration)

> Bare `/spec`, `/code`, `/review` route **directly** to the language-specific subagent — no Orchestrator. Use for quick, single-phase tasks.

| Shortcut | `subagent_type` | First action: read agent file | Constraint |
|----------|-----------------|-------------------------------|------------|
| `/spec` | `generalPurpose` | `.cursor/agents/spec-{lang}.md` | Plan files ONLY |
| `/code` | `generalPurpose` | `.cursor/agents/code-{lang}.md` | Code edits ONLY; plan MUST exist |
| `/review` | `generalPurpose` | `.cursor/agents/review-{lang}.md` | Review report ONLY |

**Routing:** Supervisor spawns `Task(subagent_type: "generalPurpose")` directly. The subagent reads its `.cursor/agents/{phase}-{lang}.md` file as its first action. No Orchestrator wrapper.

**Output Constraints are HARD rules.** Spec Agent MUST NOT edit source code. Code Agent MUST NOT proceed without a plan. Violations require revert and re-routing.

### ➤ SECURITY TRACK

| Shortcut | Agent | Inference Trigger |
|----------|-------|-------------------|
| `/sec [slug]` | Security Agent (`agent-security.md`) | "security scan", "audit vulnerabilities", "SAST", "SCA", "CVE" |

### ➤ DAC TRACK (Diagrams-as-Code)

**Structurizr DSL** (default when using `--dac` without `--excalidraw` / `--e`):

| Shortcut | Alias | Agent | Constraint |
|----------|-------|-------|------------|
| `/dac spec` | `/spec --dac` | `agent-spec-dac.md` (Cartographer) | Spec files ONLY |
| `/dac code` | `/code --dac` | `agent-coding-dac.md` (Draftsman) | DSL edits ONLY |
| `/dac review` | `/review --dac` | `agent-review-dac.md` (Inspector) | Review report ONLY |
| `/dac deploy` | *(none)* | `agent-ops-dac-deploy.md` (Publisher) | Structurizr deployment ONLY — **no `--excalidraw` / `--e`** |

**Excalidraw JSON** — append **`--excalidraw`** or **`--e`** to `/dac spec|code|review` (or use `/spec|code|review --dac --excalidraw`). Slim prompt: `.cursor/agents/excalidraw-dac.md`; canonical protocol: `docs/_ai_system/agents/agent-excalidraw-dac.md`; style: `docs/_ai_system/standards/excalidraw-dac-style.md`.

| Shortcut | Alias | Agent | Constraint |
|----------|-------|-------|------------|
| `/dac spec --excalidraw` | `/dac spec --e`, `/spec --dac --excalidraw` | `excalidraw-dac.md` → `agent-excalidraw-dac.md` (Spec section) | Diagram change specification ONLY |
| `/dac code --excalidraw` | `/dac code --e`, `/code --dac --excalidraw` | `excalidraw-dac.md` → `agent-excalidraw-dac.md` (Code section) | `.excalidraw` JSON edits ONLY |
| `/dac review --excalidraw` | `/dac review --e`, `/review --dac --excalidraw` | `excalidraw-dac.md` → `agent-excalidraw-dac.md` (Review section) | Review report + plan verification ONLY |

### ➤ TESTING TRACK

| Shortcut | Agent | Inference Trigger | Constraint |
|----------|-------|-------------------|------------|
| `/test [target]` | Test Agent (`agent-test-python.md`) | "test api", "probe", "integration test" | Cannot modify app source |
| `/test codify` | Test Agent (codify mode) | "codify tests", "formalize tests" | Cannot modify app source |

### ➤ DOCUMENTATION TRACK

| Shortcut | Agent | Shortcut | Agent |
|----------|-------|----------|-------|
| `/docs-user` | User Guide Agent | `/docs-dev` | Dev Doc Agent |
| `/report` | Weekly Report Agent (`agent-report.md`); first action `.cursor/agents/report.md` | `/roadmap` | Roadmap Agent |

**Routing for `/report`:** Direct (not orchestrated). Supervisor spawns `Task(subagent_type: "generalPurpose")`; first action: read `.cursor/agents/report.md`, then canonical `docs/_ai_system/agents/agent-report.md`.

### ➤ OPERATIONS TRACK

| Shortcut | Agent | Shortcut | Agent |
|----------|-------|----------|-------|
| `/onboard [project-name]` | Onboard Agent (`agent-ops-onboard.md` — **M1-P8**) | `/update` / `/update [project-name]` | Update Agent (`agent-ops-update.md`) |
| `/jira` | Jira Agent | `/feedback [msg]` | Feedback Agent |
| `/tune [agent]` | System Tuning | — | — |

### Full Lifecycle

**Orchestrated** (`/o`): Spec → Code (self-correction loop) → Review → QA → QA Resilience. QA is mandatory per protocol unless the active agent file documents a hub-only exception. Auto-chains unless `--pause` or circuit breaker. Remediation loops (max 3) run autonomously. The flow is NOT complete until both QA phases have executed.

**Direct** (`/spec`, `/code`, `/review`): Single-phase only. User manages phase transitions manually.

---

## 3. CONTEXT ISOLATION

Context isolation is mandatory. In Orchestrated mode (`/o`), each phase runs in its own Task subagent. In Direct mode (`/spec`, `/code`, `/review`), single-phase execution naturally isolates.

### Violation Recovery
If the AI has already acted without completing routing: stop immediately, revert changes outside the agent's Output Constraints, re-run the full routing protocol, and acknowledge the error.

---

