## 5. DECISION TRACEABILITY

Every request echoes the Supervisor Decision block (Section 0). With `--trace`: adds section-level tracking, persistent trace files per `debug-protocol.md`, and deep review gate. Agents must receive, append to, and include the `Rules Consulted` list in all output.

---

## 6. MCP TOOL DEPENDENCIES — Hard Stop on Failure

Cuebert registers four MCP servers in `.cursor/mcp.json`: **`cuebert-core`** (sets `CUEBERT_MEMORY_MODE=text`), **`cuebert-asset`**, **`cuebert-engine`**, **`cuebert-qa`**. Non-cuebert servers are out of scope for this hub.

The `sequentialthinking` gate is enforced at two levels:

1. **Supervisor Pre-Dispatch Probe (Step 0.9):** Before dispatching any `/spec`, `/code`, `/review`, or `/sec` subagent, the Supervisor MUST call `sequentialthinking` with a health-check thought. If this fails, hard stop — do NOT spawn the subagent. Visually confirm the four `cuebert-*` entries are enabled in Settings > MCP alongside `sequential-thinking`.
2. **Subagent First Action:** Every Spec, Code, Review, and Security subagent begins with a `sequentialthinking` call as its first action.

**Hard Stop Rule:** If `sequentialthinking` is unavailable at either level, the system MUST abort and surface the error:
> ⛔ HARD STOP: `sequentialthinking` MCP server is unavailable. No work will be performed. Check Settings > MCP for the `sequential-thinking` server status.

Silent fallback to inline reasoning is **explicitly forbidden**. This was added after the MCP server silently failed for an extended period without any user notification.

> **Polyglot expansion:** As new languages and tracks land, routing tables in `.cursor/rules/cuebert-supervisor.mdc` and new `.mdc` rule files will be documented in `docs/_ai_system/` (M4–M6+).
